<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yang Xiuqing</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1821">1821</a>–<a href="/years/1856">1856</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as East King</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yang Xiuqing was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiping-rebellion">Taiping Rebellion</a>, holding the title East King and acting as chief military and administrative commander of the Taiping Heavenly Kingdom. He claimed to speak with the voice of God the Father, and his growing ambition led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-xiuquan">Hong Xiuquan</a> to have him killed in the Tianjing Incident of 1856.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yang-xiuqing.jpg" alt="Yang Xiuqing" width="320" height="547" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Perinbaba · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%9D%A8%E7%A7%80%E6%B8%85.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
